  "raw_text": "The privacy gate was redesigned to fail closed rather than silently defaulting off. The gate now reads a strict tristate \u2014 on, off, or unset \u2014 and enforces protection for sensitive off-box calls under on, unset, and any unrecognized value, relaxing only when PRIVACY_GATE is explicitly set to off. The motivating concern was that running a private corpus while forgetting to set the variable would leak data; under the safe default, forgetting protects the data instead. This makes PRIVACY_GATE=off a conscious, deliberate decision to send data to the cloud rather than an accidental state.",
